Z||000011||mrfixit58||05-21-2001||04:00 PM||||mrfiero - he he he. I was on a business trip to Colorado Springs a few years back. It was 70 degrees in Denver when we arrived on Saturday morning. Sunny all day. The next morning, there was 4" of snow on the ground and I drove through a raging blizzard from Colorado Springs to Denver. Truly an amazing experience.<P>Fierohoho - I was stationed in Grand Forks, North Dakota for three and a half years. In 1977, we had a blizzard to bad that no one could leave the barracks for three days (good thing each room has a refrigerator). During the worst of the storm, there were warnings on the TV that any exposed skin would flash freeze in 18 seconds. Flat spots on tires... yea, I remember. And just think, a few months before I'd never even seen snow.<P>Todays weather forecast in sunny Tampa, Florida... hot, 20% chance, humidity is rising, drought conditions still prevail.<P><P>------------------<BR>Roy :D<BR>87 GT  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/pennocksize.JPG"> ||||reg||6
